> I tested it again, and it seems to happen randomly.

The error occurs when `selected_scene` is not valid, but there is an `if` to check for it, so I don't know how the program bypasses it.
```c++
		if (selected_scene && !instance) {
			instance = Object::cast_to<Node2D>(selected_scene->duplicate());
```

> * I don't think we need another set of grid settings, the one in the snap menu should probably be used instead. And if the scene painter tool is enabled with the grid enabled, we should force-show this grid.

@groud Sorry to ask, but I mean, should I delete the grid completely or just the settings section? For example, when the tool is activated, it should come and use the canvas item grid and the canvas item snap for snapping.
If you explain in more detail, I will be better able to understand what scenario you are considering.
